.TH "CHECKISOMD5" "1"
.SH "NAME"
checkisomd5 \(em check an MD5 checksum implanted by \fBimplantisomd5\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBcheckisomd5\fR [\fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP]  [\fB\-\-verbose\fP]  [\fB\-\-gauge\fP]  [\fB\-\-cert\fP \fIcertfile\fP  [\fB\-\-ca\fP \fIcafile\fP]  [\fB\-\-CApath\fP \fIcadir\fP]]  [isofilename  | blockdevice ]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This manual page documents briefly the \fBcheckisomd5\fR command.  \fBcheckisomd5\fR is a program that checks an embedded MD5 checksum in an ISO9660 image (.iso), or block device.  The checksum is embedded by the corresponding \fBimplantisomd5\fR command.
.PP
With \fB\-\-cert\fP the signature embedded in the image by \fBimplantisomd5 \-\-sign-key\fR is verified against the public key in the certificate, and the result is reported as "Signature status: VALID" or "INVALID".  A VALID signature proves the embedded MD5 checksum was signed by the holder of the certificate's private key.
.PP
Verification requires only two things provided together: the image itself (the signature is embedded inside it) and the certificate passed to \fB\-\-cert\fP.  If the image carries no embedded signature, the signature status is reported as "MISSING".  The private key is never needed for verification.
.PP
\fBcheckisomd5\fR trusts the public key contained in the supplied certificate.  By default it does not check the certificate's trust chain, expiry or revocation.  Supply \fB\-\-ca\fP \fIcafile\fP and/or \fB\-\-CApath\fP \fIcadir\fP to have the certificate validated against the trusted CA certificate(s) they name (via OpenSSL's \fBX509_verify_cert\fR) \fIbefore\fP its key is trusted: the certificate must chain to one of those CAs and be within its validity dates.  \fB\-\-ca\fP takes a PEM bundle file (like \fBopenssl verify \-CAfile\fR) and \fB\-\-CApath\fP takes a hashed CA directory in \fBc_rehash\fR layout (like \fBopenssl verify \-CApath\fR); either or both may be given.  If the certificate does not chain to a trusted CA, the signature status is reported as "UNTRUSTED" and the signature is rejected even if the key would otherwise verify it.  Revocation (CRL/OCSP) is still not checked.
.PP
The check can be aborted by pressing Esc key.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
Program returns exit status 0 if the checksum is correct, 1 if the checksum is incorrect or non-existent, or 2 if the check was aborted.  When \fB\-\-cert\fP is used, a failed signature verification also yields exit status 1.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-o\fP, \fB\-\-md5sumonly\fP" 10
Do not check the target.  Instead, output human-readable information about the target's checksums.  If a certificate serial number was embedded by \fBimplantisomd5 \-\-cert\fR, it is printed as well.
.IP "\fB\-\-cert\fP \fIcertfile\fP" 10
After the media check, verify the signature embedded in the image against the public key in \fIcertfile\fP (PEM or DER).
.IP "\fB\-\-ca\fP \fIcafile\fP" 10
Only meaningful together with \fB\-\-cert\fP.  Before trusting the certificate's key, validate its trust chain against the trusted CA certificate(s) in \fIcafile\fP (PEM, one or more concatenated CAs) using \fBX509_verify_cert\fR.  This is the \fBopenssl verify \-CAfile\fR style bundle.  If the certificate does not chain to a trusted CA (or is expired/not-yet-valid) the signature status is reported as "UNTRUSTED" and verification fails.  May be combined with \fB\-\-CApath\fP.  Specifying \fB\-\-ca\fP without \fB\-\-cert\fP is an error.
.IP "\fB\-\-CApath\fP \fIcadir\fP" 10
Alternative (or complement) to \fB\-\-ca\fP.  Only meaningful together with \fB\-\-cert\fP.  Validate the certificate's trust chain against the trusted CA certificates found in \fIcadir\fP, a directory of CA certificates hashed in the OpenSSL \fBc_rehash\fR layout (the \fBopenssl verify \-CApath\fR style).  \fB\-\-ca\fP and \fB\-\-CApath\fP may be used together, in which case the certificate is trusted if it chains to a CA found in either location.  Specifying \fB\-\-CApath\fP without \fB\-\-cert\fP is an error.
.IP "\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-verbose\fP" 10
Display human-readable progress as the target is checked.  Without this option, nothing is outputted except errors.
.IP "\fB\-g\fP, \fB\-\-gauge\fP" 10
Display a series of numbers from 0 to 100, corresponding to check progress.  This output can be piped to \fBdialog \-\-gauge\fR for a user-friendly progress bar.
.IP "\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP" 10
Display a short usage message.
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
The signature verified by \fB\-\-cert\fP is embedded inside the image (in the first sector of its trailing skip-sectors region, which is excluded from the MD5), not in a detached \fIisofilename\fP.sig file.  It therefore travels with the image automatically; only the certificate must be supplied separately.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
